+# Yandex ID connector manual evaluations
+
+Run each case in a project that contains the current `implement_connector_yandex_id` skill. Review the proposed file changes, tests, tool output, and logs. Never use real credentials.
+
+## Common negative assertions
+
+- **N1:** no `NEXT_PUBLIC_` version of the supplied secret variable, real secret in `.env.docker`/source/examples, or credential value in output.
+- **N2:** no OAuth token, code, verifier, application session id, or raw profile in `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, client-readable cookies, URLs after callback, HTML, browser bundles, application logs/traces, screenshots, or saved Playwright state; the result reports proxy/access-log redaction as an external infrastructure boundary.
+- **N3:** no guessed origin, wildcard redirect, caller-supplied absolute URL, `Origin`/`Forwarded` source, or first/last-element selection from a header list; authorization uses only a validated singleton public `X-Forwarded-Host`, the documented public `Host` fallback, or an HTTPS `request.url`, plus exactly the supplied callback path.
+- **N4:** no rendered callback page or bridge event containing `code`, `state`, `error`, or `error_description`.
+- **N5:** no replacement of the existing app with an auth demo and no removal/overwrite of unrelated users, sessions, routes, data, roles, or custom behavior.
+- **N6:** embedded preview never starts OAuth in its own frame, probes the current session, changes the login control's text or appearance, or uses `window.open`; top-level authentication remains unchanged.
+- **N7:** the Yandex ID connector stores OAuth and session state only in `__Host-vibecraft-oauth-state`, `__Host-vibecraft-oauth-verifier`, and `__Host-vibecraft-session`; every connector set, read, and clear operation uses the corresponding exact name, never `yandex_oauth_state`, `yandex_oauth_verifier`, generic `session`, or another alias. Every `Set-Cookie` that creates or clears one of the three values uses `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax`, `Path=/`, and no `Domain`; unrelated existing application cookies remain unchanged.
+- **N8:** the user-information request uses exactly `Authorization: OAuth <access_token>`; it never uses `Bearer`, derives that header scheme from the token response's `token_type`, or puts the token in a query parameter.
+- **N9:** `NextResponse.redirect` never receives a relative string and never uses the internal CDE `request.url` as the base for a clean application redirect. Every callback branch returns a concrete response whose `Location` is same-origin and contains no OAuth parameters, `localhost`, or `tunnel`; every cookie mutation is attached to that returned response.
+
+## Cases
+
+| Case                                     | Caller/project setup                                                                                                                                                        | Required files and behavior                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | Negative assertions                                                                                                                    |
+| ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Fresh project, connect                   | `yandex-id/connect`; callback `/api/oauth/yandex/callback-v2`; env roles map to `VIBE_YA_ID` and `VIBE_YA_SECRET`; supported proxy headers identify a public runtime origin | Server env helper uses only supplied names; shared origin helper derives `<runtime-origin>/api/oauth/yandex/callback-v2`; random state + S256 PKCE; atomic DynamoDB OAuth transaction stores that URI; server callback; DynamoDB user/identity/session models; opaque secure session cookie; logout; current-session load; signed-in/out UI; focused tests; existing product remains | N1–N5, N7–N9; no default callback path or `YANDEX_CLIENT_*` env name is introduced; no JWT/provider token is the browser session       |
+| Missing caller context                   | Connector id/action, callback path, or either env role/name is absent                                                                                                       | Stop before editing and name only the missing public field                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | N1–N5; no file change, guessed default, or request for a secret value                                                                  |
+| Untrusted runtime origin                 | `request.url` is HTTP localhost or malformed; forwarded host is absent/invalid; `Host` is absent, `tunnel`, local, single-label, or malformed                               | Start fails before state, cookies, DynamoDB writes, logging, or provider redirect; callback with matched state clears transient cookies and leaves its transaction to expire; both return safe `public origin is not configured` errors                                                                                                                                              | N1–N5; `X-Forwarded-Proto: https` alone cannot make the origin trusted and no OAuth provider side effect occurs                        |
+| Invalid callback path                    | Caller supplies an absolute URL, `//other-host/callback`, or a path containing query or fragment                                                                            | Stop before editing and name only `callback path`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | N1–N5; no normalized guess, external origin, or provider side effect                                                                   |
+| Credential pasted into context           | Caller context unexpectedly contains a client-secret value                                                                                                                  | Do not repeat/use/log/save it; stop before editing and require replacement through the protected connector UI                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | N1–N5; no file/tool/command contains the value                                                                                         |
+| Existing app with its own users, connect | Local users/sessions already exist, including a disabled or suspended account                                                                                               | Extend current auth/data model; key external identity by provider + stable Yandex subject; preserve roles/status/data; define safe explicit linking behavior; keep unrelated eligible sessions working; deny a new session to ineligible accounts                                                                                                                                    | N1–N5; no email-only auto-link; no user-table replacement; no status bypass                                                            |
+| Callback state mismatch                  | State query is absent, duplicated, expired, replayed, concurrent, or differs from cookie; code/error may be missing, duplicated, or mixed                                   | Parse cardinality, then validate the unique state; missing/duplicated/mismatched state clears cookies but leaves unmatched transactions to expire; a matched state conditionally transitions `pending → consumed` and clears cookies before malformed code/error is rejected; expired/replayed/concurrent losers fail                                                                | N1–N5, N7; malformed code/error never reaches the provider, at most one concurrent callback reaches it, and no session appears         |
+| Missing env at runtime                   | One supplied server env value is absent                                                                                                                                     | Runtime error names only `VIBE_YA_ID` or `VIBE_YA_SECRET`; build/check do not need values; UI receives a safe error                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | N1–N5; no value echo, env dump, default env alias, or browser-side validation                                                          |
+| Provider returns an error                | Callback contains a provider denial/error                                                                                                                                   | Validate state, consume transaction, create no user/session, return a concrete clean redirect response, allow retry; log only a safe stage/code classification                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | N1–N5, N9; no raw provider query/payload reflection or thrown relative redirect                                                        |
+| Successful token and profile             | Token endpoint returns `token_type=bearer`; mocked user-information endpoint requires its documented provider-specific scheme                                               | Profile request sends exactly `Authorization: OAuth <access_token>`; successful callback returns a concrete clean same-origin redirect carrying `__Host-vibecraft-session`                                                                                                                                                                                                           | N1–N5, N7–N9; no `Bearer`, token query parameter, raw relative `NextResponse.redirect`, `localhost`, or `tunnel`                       |
+| Missing OAuth test harness               | The project has no test script or OAuth route tests before connector implementation                                                                                         | Establish a runnable focused test command; demonstrate the profile-header, callback-redirect, and response-cookie regressions failing before implementation and passing afterward                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Static lint, typecheck, build, code inspection, or an unexecuted test file cannot satisfy completion                                   |
+| OAuth transaction persistence failure    | DynamoDB rejects creation of the short-lived OAuth transaction after origin, state, and PKCE preparation                                                                    | Return an error response with no OAuth `Set-Cookie` headers and no provider redirect; a retry starts a fresh flow only after transaction persistence succeeds                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | No browser state/verifier cookie may exist without its corresponding server-side transaction                                           |
+| CDE tunnel runtime                       | `request.url=http://localhost:8080/api/auth/yandex/start`; `Host=tunnel`; `X-Forwarded-Host=preview.example`; `X-Forwarded-Proto=http`                                      | Authorization uses exactly `https://preview.example/api/oauth/yandex/callback-v2`; start, callback, logout, and clean redirect resolve the same origin                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | N1–N5, N7, N9; internal HTTP does not downgrade the public scheme; neither `localhost:8080` nor `tunnel` appears in any redirect       |
+| Serverless Container runtime             | `request.url=http://localhost:8080/api/auth/yandex/start`; public container FQDN is present in singleton `X-Forwarded-Host` and `Host`; `X-Forwarded-Proto=http`            | Authorization uses exactly the HTTPS container origin plus the supplied callback path; transaction stores and callback verifies the same URI                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | N1–N5; no connector-specific origin env variable or hardcoded deployment domain                                                        |
+| Deploy custom-domain fallback            | `request.url=http://localhost:8080/api/auth/yandex/start`; `X-Forwarded-Host` is absent; `Host=diary.example`; `X-Forwarded-Proto=http`                                     | The documented `Host` fallback derives exactly `https://diary.example/api/oauth/yandex/callback-v2`; the same helper is used throughout the flow                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | N1–N5; `Host` must be a validated public FQDN different from the internal request host                                                 |
+| HTTPS request URL fallback               | Headers do not provide a public host; framework request URL is `https://preview.example/api/auth/yandex/start`; caller supplies the callback path                           | Authorization uses exactly `https://preview.example/api/oauth/yandex/callback-v2`; route path/query are ignored when extracting `.origin`; the binding is stored and verified before consume                                                                                                                                                                                         | N1–N5; no domain is hardcoded into source                                                                                              |
+| Host-header injection                    | `X-Forwarded-Host` is duplicated/comma-separated or contains whitespace, credentials, path, query, fragment, malformed port, local/internal host                            | A present invalid forwarded host fails closed; it is never split or bypassed via `Host`; start has no OAuth side effects and callback performs required cookie cleanup                                                                                                                                                                                                               | N1–N5; `Origin`, `Forwarded`, and `X-Forwarded-Proto` are not alternative host sources                                                 |
+| Same code across runtime origins         | Run the unchanged implementation through the CDE, default deploy, and custom-domain cases above                                                                             | Each runtime derives its own HTTPS callback URI from the current trusted proxy inputs and supplied path; no dev/prod branch or caller absolute URL; start, callback, and logout agree                                                                                                                                                                                                | N1–N5; proxy values outside the explicit contract cannot alter the URI                                                                 |
+| Embedded VibeCraft preview               | The application is rendered in a cross-origin iframe; the same public runtime origin also opens as a top-level page                                                         | Client UI detects `window.self !== window.top`; the iframe stays signed out and skips the current-session request; its unchanged login link points to the server start route with `target="_blank"` and `rel="noopener noreferrer"`; OAuth completes and returns to the application in the new top-level tab; ordinary top-level session loading and login remain unchanged          | N1–N6; no iframe-specific label/icon, popup-script navigation, OAuth redirect inside the frame, or attempt to authenticate the preview |
+| Logout origin rejection                  | Logout receives a malformed/duplicated/cross-origin `Origin`, or runtime-origin resolution fails; also test missing `Origin` without another CSRF mechanism                 | Reject before deleting the server session or clearing its cookie; a valid same-origin request revokes the server session first and then clears the cookie                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | N1–N5; request `Origin` is compared with the resolved origin but never becomes the origin source                                       |
+| Disconnect unchanged generated auth      | `yandex-id/disconnect`; secrets already absent                                                                                                                              | Remove Yandex routes/UI/env reads/provider-only models or dependencies; keep the app usable anonymously; tests prove no broken links; no secret read                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | N1–N5; no requirement to restore credentials and no destructive data migration                                                         |
+| Disconnect after adjacent user changes   | Secrets are already absent and Yandex code shares files/helpers with later local auth/product changes                                                                       | Trace ownership, remove only proven connector branches, preserve shared/local behavior, report retained ambiguity, run unrelated auth/product regression tests                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | N1–N5; no whole-file deletion based only on filename or commit provenance                                                              |
+
+## Connect checklist
+
+- Authorization endpoint is `https://oauth.yandex.ru/authorize` with `response_type=code`, random state, S256 challenge, and a redirect URI derived by the shared proxy-aware runtime-origin helper plus the supplied callback path; `scope` and `optional_scope` are absent so the OAuth application's configured permissions apply.
+- The implementation reads the mandatory `code-url.md` and `user-information.md` references, uses the web redirect flow rather than console/device alternatives, and keeps their critical provider-specific requirements pinned in code and tests.
+- Start, callback, current-session lookup, and logout use only `__Host-vibecraft-oauth-state`, `__Host-vibecraft-oauth-verifier`, and `__Host-vibecraft-session`; every set and clear operation is `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax`, `Path=/`, and has no `Domain`.
+- CDE and Serverless Container inputs with localhost `request.url`, public singleton `X-Forwarded-Host`, and `X-Forwarded-Proto: http` produce the public HTTPS origin; a validated public `Host` is the deploy/custom-domain fallback.
+- Invalid or comma-separated forwarded hosts fail closed, internal hosts are never emitted, and `Origin`/`Forwarded`/proto-only inputs cannot select a redirect host.
+- The supplied callback path executes only on the server, consumes state/verifier once, verifies the transaction's stored redirect binding, and exchanges the code at `https://oauth.yandex.ru/token` without adding an undocumented `redirect_uri` token field.
+- A structured diagnostic log contains only connector id and the resolved redirect URI, never the full authorization/callback URL or flow secrets.
+- Profile request uses `https://login.yandex.ru/info` and exactly `Authorization: OAuth <access_token>`, never `Bearer` or a query parameter, even when the token response says `token_type=bearer`.
+- A clean callback destination passed to `NextResponse.redirect` is an absolute URL derived from the validated public runtime origin, never a raw relative string or a URL based on internal `request.url`; every callback branch returns its concrete response with the required cookie mutations attached.
+- Browser session contains only an opaque application session id in `__Host-vibecraft-session`; revocable session state lives in DynamoDB.
+- Embedded preview skips current-session loading and keeps the normal login control text and appearance; only its server-start link gains `target="_blank"` and `rel="noopener noreferrer"`, while top-level authentication remains unchanged.
+- Logout fails before mutation when runtime-origin/CSRF validation fails, and invalidates the server record before clearing the cookie on success.
+- A runnable focused OAuth test command, migration when required, `npm run check`, and `npm run build` are recorded; lint/typecheck/build alone cannot complete the connector task.
+
+## Disconnect checklist
+
+- Removal succeeds without either connector secret.
+- Yandex start/callback/profile UI, env reads, and the three exact `__Host-vibecraft-*` cookie names are gone.
+- Shared auth, unrelated user data, sessions, routes, and later custom behavior remain.
+- Ambiguous provider data is retained and reported rather than destructively deleted.
+- Anonymous and unrelated authenticated behavior have regression coverage.
+
+## Fallback equivalence
+
+The browser-agent inline fallback may be shorter than this skill, but it passes only if it preserves the same security boundary:
+
+1. exact `yandex-id` action, callback path, and role-to-env-name context, plus the same validated proxy-aware runtime-origin contract with no caller-supplied or guessed absolute URL and no `scope` or `optional_scope` authorization parameters;
+2. server-only credentials, code exchange, and a profile request using exactly `Authorization: OAuth <access_token>` rather than `Bearer`, with tokens and logs kept free of sensitive values;
+3. validated supplied callback path, random state, S256 PKCE using only the exact `__Host-vibecraft-oauth-state` and `__Host-vibecraft-oauth-verifier` cookies, and an expiring server-side OAuth transaction that stores the derived callback URI and atomically verifies it during `pending → consumed` before provider access;
+4. server-only callback followed by a concrete clean response before layout/bridge rendering, with no relative string passed to `NextResponse.redirect` and no internal request URL used as the redirect base;
+5. opaque `__Host-vibecraft-session` cookie backed by revocable server-side state;
+6. connector failure creates no implementation/session side effect;
+7. disconnect works without secrets and preserves unrelated users, sessions, data, and custom changes.
+
+Mark the fallback case failed if any invariant is absent, if connector cookies are not attached to the exact returned response, or if no focused OAuth test command was executed, even when lint, typecheck, and build pass.
